Practical 3
Service + Dependency Injection
Aim:
To create a service and use dependency injection in Angular.
Steps:

Step 1: Create Service
ng generate service student

Step 2: Write Code in student.service.ts
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
@Injectable({
providedIn: 'root'
})
export class StudentService {
getStudent() {
return 'Student Name: Amit';
}
}

Step 3: Use Service in app.component.ts
import { StudentService } from './student.service';
export class AppComponent {
name = '';
constructor(private studentService: StudentService) {
this.name = this.studentService.getStudent();
}
}

Step 4: Display Data in app.component.html
<h3>{{ name }}</h3>

Output:
Student data fetched from service and displayed.

Result:
Thus, service and dependency injection are implemented successfully.
